      "jcr:created": "Wed Oct 02 2019 19:05:16 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Course code: 4295</span></p>\n<p>2 contact hours</p>\n<p>Nurses</p>\n<p>SPD<br>\n</p>\n<p>This education program clarifies the Spaulding Classification system and explains why some infection prevention experts are asking for revisions to the classification definitions. An overview of low-temperature sterilization processes will be discussed, as well as differentiating the hydrogen peroxide sterilization process from the liquid chemical sterilant process and the high-level disinfection process. The program will also include an explanation of the hazards of ethylene oxide and legal requirements for using ethylene oxide sterilization.<br>\n</p>\n",
